 ### Space Skipping with 3DDDA
-A mechanism to skip empty regions in sparse volume data using a uniform grid and 3DDDA algorithm [S3]. The fragment shader traverses the macrocell grid using 3DDDA in an outer loop. If a macrocell is nonempty, it enters the volume rendering loop with peak finding tests between samples. To begin sampling, it finds the first $t$ to sample when entering a macrocell by solving for the maximum $x$ after $T_{enter}$: $x_{tenter} = (-b + \sqrt{b^2 + 2aT_{enter}})/a$. It then computes floor values and samples as in Equation 17 of [S3]. Coarse grids (64^3 cells) work best on GPU [S3].
