 ### Adaptive Ray Marching with Occupancy Grid
-A variant that uses a bitfield occupancy grid to skip empty space [S4, unofficial]. For each ray, it iterates through spatial steps. It checks occupancy using a bitfield: `sity_bitfield[ti.u32(idx//8)] & (1 << ti.u32(idx%8))`. If occupied, it stores position, direction, time, and delta into buffers and marks for network evaluation. If not occupied, it calculates the distance to the next grid boundary using `txyz = (((nxyz+0.5+0.5*ti.math.sign(ray_d))*grid_size_inv*2-1)*mip_bound-xyz)*d_inv` and advances time to skip empty space until the next boundary is reached [S4, unofficial].
